WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.410
To learn languages,

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.570
we have to master the basics.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.130
Is it true? No.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.080
Breaking news:

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.510
It is not possible to master the basics, especially at the beginning.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.820
We are going to continue making the same mistakes for a long time.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:24.840
So we don't have to worry about this useless desire to master the basics.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.759
What are the basics?

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:30.689
And I say this from my experience as a language learner.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.530
What are the basics?

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.030
Words, for example, what are basic words?

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.080
Many books that teach languages ​​start with, I

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.610
don't know, colors, numbers, but those things are very difficult.

00:00:44.725 --> 00:00:49.735
There are words with more frequency, but in any case,

00:00:49.885 --> 00:00:53.455
we will find these words with high frequency.

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:57.325
So, we'll learn those words more easily.

00:00:57.325 --> 00:01:03.805
But certain words are still going to be difficult to remember,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.135
right? The same thing with structures.

00:01:07.195 --> 00:01:11.965
For me, for example, now I am speaking in Spanish, which I don't do much.

00:01:12.055 --> 00:01:12.865
So I'm going to

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:14.745
Make basic mistakes.

00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:19.485
But if I talk more, then I would make fewer basic mistakes, right?

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:25.005
So the basics are a very subjective concept.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:31.244
And in any case, there is a natural order of acquisition of a language

00:01:31.365 --> 00:01:33.524
according to what

00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:39.554
Steven Krashen has done, for example, and this natural order of acquisition can depend

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:45.045
on the language we are learning and our language.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.270
For example, an Italian who is learning Spanish,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.730
well it will be easier, right?

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.380
Many things about grammar

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.120
and also the words are similar to words or structures in Italian.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:02.410
So, there is a natural order that is different, but for someone who is

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:07.240
learning, for example, English, we all know that in English, the

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:12.730
third person present has an "S", for example, i go, you go, I GOES.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:14.775
But this is very difficult.

00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:23.085
It's a basic grammatical thing, but non-natives continue to make

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:30.615
this very simple mistake because we have to build new habits.

00:02:30.735 --> 00:02:33.885
And this is done according to a natural order.

00:02:34.245 --> 00:02:36.255
It is done throughout a long period of time, right?

00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:42.015
So deliberately trying to learn, to master the basics

00:02:42.554 --> 00:02:47.774
is useless and not helpful, because all the time we are trying

00:02:47.774 --> 00:02:52.785
to learn, for example, conjugations, is time that I am not going

00:02:53.380 --> 00:03:00.839
to use to listen more, read more, speak more, so that my brain

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.989
gets used to the new language.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:09.929
And for that reason, on LingQ, for example, I always start with the mini stories

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:17.250
that are easy, with a lot of repetition, and in this way an idea of ​​the language is created.

00:03:18.135 --> 00:03:24.375
Because we can finally focus on the basics AFTER we have a

00:03:24.375 --> 00:03:32.835
feel for the language and we can finally, after a lot of experience with the language,

00:03:33.494 --> 00:03:37.904
try to perfect, and not master, because we are going to

00:03:37.904 --> 00:03:40.394
continue to make mistakes.

00:03:40.695 --> 00:03:44.445
It is very important not to have a feeling of frustration.

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:49.904
If even after a long time we are making basic mistakes, because

00:03:50.024 --> 00:03:52.785
this is the case with me,

00:03:52.904 --> 00:03:56.954
I think it is the case with most people who learn languages.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:04.239
So the most important thing is to stay active, keep listening, reading, enjoying

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:07.299
the language and little by little it will improve.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:13.750
And if later you want to focus on certain aspects of vocabulary

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:19.959
or grammar, you can do that and it would be easier to assimilate those things,

00:04:20.529 --> 00:04:26.440
Explanations, patterns, because ultimately, the foundation of the language is not like

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.040
building a house with bricks.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.560
It's not like there's a foundation

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.530
And then we're going to build the second floor,

00:04:34.535 --> 00:04:37.800
Third floor. No. It's like a bowl of jello.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.750
Things come and go.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.610
We learn and we forget.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:48.030
And that is why at LingQ we do not measure student progress

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.460
because this is difficult.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.850
Sometimes we have the impression of making progress and then we don't.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.310
But what we can measure

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.090
And the most important thing is the level of activity of each one.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:05.400
And if the student continues to be active, listening, reading, over time,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:12.120
using the language, with a positive attitude, it is certain that he will progress.

00:05:12.475 --> 00:05:18.205
So my advice, as a person who has learned

00:05:18.205 --> 00:05:23.335
many languages ​​at different levels, is that we cannot master the basic things.

00:05:23.335 --> 00:05:28.405
You have to continue studying, read interesting things. And little by little

00:05:28.705 --> 00:05:34.945
We are going to get used to the new language, without bothering ourselves with this

00:05:34.945 --> 00:05:37.495
desire to master the basics.

00:05:37.645 --> 00:05:38.215
See you later.

